Ladybird applies the root element’s scrollbar-color to the viewport’s
scrollbar by reading it from the root element’s box when it paints that
scrollbar. And WebKit does just the same, in its LocalFrameView::
scrollbarColorStyle(), which resolves the colors from the document
element renderer’s style. So does Gecko, whose nsLayoutUtils::
StyleForScrollbar() uses the root element’s style for the viewport’s
scrollbar. Blink instead copies the value into the LayoutView’s style,
in StyleResolver::PropagateStyleToViewport(), along with scrollbar-width
and scrollbar-gutter. So all three engines give the viewport’s scrollbar
the root element’s colors.
